    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0655" n="553" xml:id="pg553"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12593: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-24T11:00:00+08:00">December 24, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 24—4:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>929. The following telegram has been received from Vice Consul at Foochow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 23, 6 p.m. Nanking government plane bombed Foochow this
                            afternoon at 3 o’clock, apparently aiming at the aviation field which is
                            outside the city, and military headquarters within the native city.
                            Reported that four bombs were dropped and several casualties
                            resulted.</p>
                        <p>This bombing without warning was contrary to the assurances given Peck by
                            Hsu Mo.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Peck at Nanking has been instructed to bring the report to the attention of the
                    Foreign Office in the same manner Changchow bombing reported in my telegram to
                    the Department No. 928 of December 23, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
